{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01113VUfg36NQXQVVF8MQsCv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A single-folder personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings). Markdown files are the source of truth â€” `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files (academic/commercial/family/writing), plus cancelled/saved archives â€” with no database and no binary formats.\n\n- **Ships a local web app, `anchor_gui.py`** (the declared deliverable): a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders the full dashboard on every request and writes changes directly back to the markdown. It runs persistently on `http://localhost:8777` as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on host PUTER/`gwl-server`.\n\n- **Manages a task lifecycle** â€” Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored â€” interactively in the browser and via a mirrored CLI (`anchor.py`: done/cancel/save/restore/add/capture/dashboard), both sharing the same markdown format.\n\n- **Has grown into a \"Mission Control\" for trio-driven R&D.** Each project gets a window that runs the trio â€” researchPrime (Research) Â· Crucible (Planning) Â· Foreman (Build) â€” as durable, isolated server-side sessions. The North Star is a calm single-screen cockpit: each lane shows its most-recent session as a tile with one honest status light (green/amber/red/grey), clicking expands an in-place summary stacked over a real terminal.\n\n- **v2 surface** adds a truthful project memory: a session model (one trio run = one session), cached+grounding-validated summaries, a Grass Catchers idea lane, deliverable declare/pin, and an interactive terminal substrate. **Built and merged to master (2026-06-11).**\n\n- **v3 \"Mission Control\"** adds **real ConPTY terminals** (via `pywinpty` â€” the one declared exception to the stdlib-only rule, lazy-imported in `pty_manager.py` only), per-session **git-worktree isolation**, a stacking window manager, thin project rows with proactive cached summaries, stage handoffs, an ephemeral deliverable preview (hard-guarded off port 8777), and Ghost World Labs branding. **Built by Foreman across 10 GREEN waves and merged to master (2026-06-12).**\n\n- **Self-verifying:** a daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every markdown file, exercises every endpoint, and walks the full v2 and v3 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, no real ConPTY, never touching the live `:8777` service or real data).\n\n*(Note: the current branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v4` and uncommitted changes suggest a v4 redesign is in progress â€” per memory, awaiting a paradigm pick before the next Crucible/build.)*"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4251,"cache_read_input_tokens":41003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4251,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31f1c257-7675-4d45-9109-fb5a98d348d5","uuid":"bcb842d4-2925-4958-8dfe-6f80b0774cf1","request_id":"req_011CbykTr5gcGEXD7q2g4NLQ"}
